[center][size=7][color=#4FAA3C][b]FRONTS & RIVALS[/b][/color][/size]
[size=5][color=#FFFFFF]A turf war for GTA V Enhanced Story Mode by Retch*[/color][/size][/center]

[size=4][color=#FFFFFF]Three rival crews hold every business in Los Santos. Take their fronts by force, staff them with your own crew, and hold them when the crews come back for them. It runs alongside the whole story, plays like part of GTA V and pauses during missions.

Inspired by The Godfather games, Saints Row and Shadow of Mordor/War.[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Getting Started[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Your first front:[/b] after Franklin's first mission, a help box points you to the Hands On Car Wash[/*]
[*][b]Taking it:[/b] beat the three Dead Kings guarding it and it's yours[/*]
[*][b]Staffing it:[/b] the car wash comes empty, and a help box shows you how to hire your first guards[/*]
[*][b]Next Step:[/b] the top line of the menu always tells you what to do next[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Fronts[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]29 real businesses:[/b] car washes, liquor stores, motels, bars, clubs, factories and more[/*]
[*][b]Taken, not bought:[/b] every front starts in a rival crew's hands, and nothing is for sale[/*]
[*][b]Three sizes:[/b] small fronts are easy, while mid-size and big fronts pay more and fight harder[/*]
[*][b]Nightly income:[/b] every front pays out at midnight[/*]
[*][b]Growing income:[/b] fronts earn more the longer you hold them and the more you own[/*]
[*][b]Upgrades:[/b] cameras, floodlights, reinforced doors and an armory, depending on the front's size[/*]
[*][b]Bigger fronts unlock:[/b] mid-size fronts at 3 fronts held, big ones at 8[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Your Crew[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Recruits:[/b] new faces every morning, each with a name, rank and four skills, rolled fresh every game[/*]
[*][b]Fair prices:[/b] $150 to $700, depending on how good they are[/*]
[*][b]Skills:[/b] Shooting, Strength, Stamina and Stealth, which grow as guards work for you[/*]
[*][b]Ranks:[/b] Recruit, Soldier, Veteran and Lieutenant, earned with time on duty and fights[/*]
[*][b]Weapons:[/b] from a knife up to a carbine rifle, with better guns unlocking at higher ranks[/*]
[*][b]Body armour:[/b] stays on for good, and guards heal and re-armour after every fight[/*]
[*][b]Patrols:[/b] half the guards walk around the building while the rest hold the door[/*]
[*][b]Bodyguards:[/b] your first at 8 fronts and a second at 14, and they follow you anywhere[/*]
[*][b]Raids:[/b] send your best guards to take a rival front without you, with the odds shown first[/*]
[*][b]Your colours:[/b] pick 1 of 19 crew colours and a style (Street, Smart, Biker or Mixed)[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Rival Crews[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][color=#3CB371][b]Dead Kings:[/b][/color] a South Los Santos street gang in forest green[/*]
[*][color=#F07F1E][b]Hellfire MC:[/b][/color] east-side bikers in orange, riding motorcycles[/*]
[*][color=#4A7BFF][b]Vinewood Elite:[/b][/color] a west-side money crew in royal blue suits[/*]
[*][b]Crew colours:[/b] every member wears their colour, so you always know who you're fighting[/*]
[*][b]Leaders:[/b] each crew has a boss and lieutenants, and anyone who escapes comes back with a grudge[/*]
[*][b]Revenge rides:[/b] their cars range from beaters to armoured luxury models, depending on how angry they are[/*]
[*][b]Turf wars:[/b] crews fight each other and take each other's fronts at night[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Street Life[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Crews on the street:[/b] they hang out, walk the block and cruise around their turf[/*]
[*][b]Your crew too:[/b] your own people hang out around the fronts you own[/*]
[*][b]Street fights:[/b] rival crews shoot it out where their turfs meet[/*]
[*][b]Police:[/b] cops chase crew cars and break up fights, and shooting them gets you a wanted level[/*]
[*][b]Street crime:[/b] now and then a mugging, carjacking or kidnapping, never too often[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Fights[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Surprise attacks:[/b] no warning, and a timer shows how long your guards can hold out[/*]
[*][b]Defend or trust:[/b] race back and fight for a bonus, or leave it to your guards[/*]
[*][b]Tougher fights:[/b] everyone has twice the usual health, so firefights last[/*]
[*][b]Takeovers:[/b] clear every soldier and the front is yours, with a building shot and the mission passed banner[/*]
[*][b]No car shortcuts:[/b] run soldiers over and the rest open fire and call in backup[/*]
[*][b]Street heat:[/b] rises with every front you take and cools each night, and hot streets mean harder fights[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Made For Story Mode[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Balanced:[/b] income and pacing match Story Mode money and length[/*]
[*][b]Pauses:[/b] everything stops during missions, cutscenes and character switches[/*]
[*][b]The Office:[/b] a GTA-style menu, opened by holding Back/View or M (or by phone with iFruitAddon2)[/*]
[*][b]Controller support:[/b] everything works on a gamepad[/*]
[*][b]Difficulty:[/b] five levels, from Relaxed to Brutal[/*]
[*][b]Messages:[/b] every alert is saved so you can read it again[/*]
[*][b]Resets:[/b] Reset All Fronts to replay the city, or Start a New Empire for a fresh story game[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Safeguards[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*][b]Outfit check:[/b] clothing is checked against your copy of the game, and anything missing is skipped[/*]
[*][b]Performance:[/b] fewer street groups when your frame rate drops[/*]
[*][b]Save copies:[/b] your empire is backed up before every update[/*]
[*][b]Online safe:[/b] the mod switches itself off in GTA Online[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[line]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Requirements[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*]GTA V Enhanced, Story Mode, BattlEye disabled[/*]
[*][url=http://www.dev-c.com/gtav/scripthookv/]Script Hook V[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/Chiheb-Bacha/ScriptHookVDotNetEnhanced/releases]Script Hook V .NET Enhanced[/url][/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/LemonUIbyLemon/LemonUI/releases]LemonUI[/url] (SHVDN3 build)[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/Bob74/iFruitAddon2/releases]iFruitAddon2[/url] (optional, adds the Office to your phone)[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Install[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list=1]
[*]Install the requirements[/*]
[*]Copy the contents of the included scripts folder into your GTA V scripts folder[/*]
[*]Start Story Mode, and after Franklin's first mission a help box points you to your first front[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Known Issues[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*]Some fronts have fewer guard posts where the street layout leaves no safe spot[/*]
[*]Not yet tested on the Legacy edition[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=6][color=#4FAA3C][b]Credits[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][list]
[*]Clothing names and IDs: [url=https://github.com/root-cause/v-clothingnames]root-cause/v-clothingnames[/url] and [url=https://github.com/root-cause/v-besttorso]root-cause/v-besttorso[/url][/*]
[*]Ped and vehicle data: [url=https://github.com/DurtyFree/gta-v-data-dumps]DurtyFree/gta-v-data-dumps[/url][/*]
[*]LemonUI, iFruitAddon2, Script Hook V and Script Hook V .NET Enhanced, which are required but not included[/*]
[/list][/color][/size]
[size=4][color=#FFFFFF][i]*AI-directed by Retch: designed, directed and playtested by Retch, with the code, data and this description written with Claude, an AI assistant from Anthropic.[/i][/color][/size]

[center][size=4][color=#FFFFFF]Source code and every release on [url=https://github.com/RetchERez/FrontsAndRivals]GitHub[/url]
Single-player only. It switches itself off in GTA Online. Free, and not affiliated with Rockstar Games.[/color][/size][/center]
